cess correlation; need maybe explain: if Death predicts your choice and goes there, fleeing is evidence but not cause; CDT sees no causal benefit? If Death's location is set by prediction, then action cannot affect Death's location, but if you stay and Death in Damascus you die; if flee and Death in Aleppo? Need if you don't know where Death will be? Need maybe not dwell. Adversarial Offer: Need explain source's example: two boxes each cost $1, seller put $3 in each box predicted not acquire, accuracy .75. Buyer can purchase one or none not both. CDT reasons at least one box contains $3? Actually if seller predicts buyer not to acquire each box independently? If buyer chooses a box, causal expected value of chosen box? Because seller's prediction about that box is correlated with buyer's choice through common cause? CDT holds fixed prediction? Need parse: seller predicted buyer not to acquire each box. If buyer considers buying box 1, under do(buy 1), probability box1 contains $3 is P(seller predicted not buy 1). If accuracy 0.75? But because can't buy both, maybe at least one predicted not acquire? Source says CDT reasons at least one box contains $3. Therefore average box at least $1.50 in causal expected value, > cost, buy one. But seller profits. Need maybe mention as alleged counterexample where CDT's causal calculation ignores selection/adversarial correlation. Need be careful not too long.\n\nNeed include mathematical definitions:\n- Decision problem: finite actions A, outcomes O, utility u:O→R, states/word variables.\n- EDT: V_EDT(a)=Σ_o u(o) P(o|a) (if P(a)>0).\n- CDT Gibbard-Harper: V_CDT(a)=Σ_o u(o) P(a □→ o) where □→ counterfactual. Or P(A -> O). Need mention probabilities of counterfactuals.\n- Imaging: Given possible worlds W, prior P, closeness ordering, define P_a(o)=Σ_{w∈W} P(w) 1[o holds at f_a(w)] where f_a(w) is closest a-world to w. Then V_CDT(a)=Σ_o u(o)P_a(o).\n- Causal model: structural causal model (U,V,F) or DAG. Intervention do(A=a) sets A